{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil","id":996624,"title":"[GotV] Crimson Veil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T08:43:08-07:00","id":996624,"title":"[GotV] Crimson Veil","content":"Topic for discussion this intense Guardians initiation to Order. So I run initiations of mage PCs in Boston setting. One of them is Guardian-to-be and I start to flash her initiation rites. Problem is that I do not have in now plot any Left Hand mages to clean for PC. What other way I can run Crimson Veil plot for character than hunting PCs enemy mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:04:35-07:00","id":996636,"title":"","content":"So you don't have local lefties, well, the Guardians are a global organization. Send her on a trip.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, run the sham version of the Crimson Veil. Have a Guardian pose as a lefty, have other Guardians leading her on in investigating him before she's handed the kill order. She just has to think she's killed the target until she's fully indoctrinated in the Guardians. The fun part of this approach is that later you can bring back the Guardian she &quot;killed&quot; for drama and plot fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 11-01-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:51:18-07:00","id":996720,"title":"","content":"The Crimson Veil doesn't need to target a serious threat, does it? Someone simply has to die. Perhaps there's a Sleeper who broke into a Mage's sanctum and now simply knows too much for the Labyrinth. Perhaps some hedge wizard is blatantly abusing magic and revealing its existence to Sleepers; a threat, even if it isn't Awakened sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:57:20-07:00","id":996728,"title":"","content":"Or some Free Council guy is careless with Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T03:05:13-07:00","id":997065,"title":"","content":"Guardians of the Veil are always balancing their duties with remaining accepted within the Pentacle. As Mages they have a variety of non-lethal methods at their disposal, especially against non-Awakened. A Caucus that starts solving minor problems with murder is jumping off the deep end and risks being purged by the other Orders. Remember that one of the Veils involves refusing an unreasonable order. A fake assassination is your best bet. If a target is truly dangerous Guardians are unlikely to send in a newbie, at least not alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T03:38:05-07:00","id":997069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=996728#post996728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or some Free Council guy is careless with Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking about this idea - Free Council seems as most going over the Paradox in Pentacle, but there is also in-cabal candidate for future Libertine.<br /> <br /> And in Boston, we have only one truly Council column ( <i>Dead Wrens</i> ) in that other PC is taking her apprenticeship - so I do not know how this could backfire...<br /> <br /> 'You killed my mentors cabalmate!'<br /> 'Well, he was overusing magic, using them irresponsibly.'<br /> 'They are bloody pirates! They kill only hangovers with their spells and steal some booty!'<br /> *Crimson Sister silence*<br /> *From 'dead guy' entering scene* 'Hi guys, I needed to run to my family as mother got sick. Sorry for not informing on this. How is going?'<br /> *Everyone confused*<br /> Curtain...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-02-2016, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T12:28:38-07:00","id":997306,"title":"","content":"Yeah, killing other Awakened is - and should be - rare. Unless the Guardians feel truly invulnerable and indomitable as a regional power, they're going to limit the edges of their blades to openly and blatantly Left-Handed practitioners, Seers, and the like. A libertine who is careless with Paradoxes is going to have to cause a lot of them before they get more than a not-so-gentle wink and nudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T16:25:12-07:00","id":997423,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> What about Blood of the Lamb? A solitary Scelestus is a perfect target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T22:38:40-07:00","id":997562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=997423#post997423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> What about Blood of the Lamb? A solitary Scelestus is a perfect target.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. <b>How, in the world, Guardians would know about him?</b> He IS hiding from other mages on purpose. Guardians are not omniscient. They can only fix what they know about.<br /> 2. <b>PCs are in Boston proper, not New England at large.</b> Also, it would be like looking for a needle in a haystack, pinging correct location of him.<br /> 3. <b>It has nothing to my main plot of chronicle</b> - Philosophers Stone, Nicholas Flamel ( on the run ), cult of False Angel Mexeriel ( in Wendell ) or Tammuz Promethean Mr. White ( in Boston ). Adding whole Scelestus hunt to this will make plot even more convulent than it's right now - and that also only 1/4 of cabal will be actively partaking.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm starting to think that Guardians should make one of them play Left-Handed for a bit</b> - but what this then teach to future Crimson Sister? That you cannot trust Guardians because every one of them can go Left-Hand? Even when they actively seek Left-Handed as Order's mission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T01:33:28-07:00","id":997604,"title":"","content":"You can't control what a PC will take away from it. Finding out is where the fun is. Still, she'd have to be pretty stupid to think that just because the Guardians occasionally kill a left-handed that it renders them immune to temptation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:30:03-07:00","id":997824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=997562#post997562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. <b>How, in the world, Guardians would know about him?</b> He IS hiding from other mages on purpose. Guardians are not omniscient. They can only fix what they know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have them find him. Why do you think he's in the book in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. <b>PCs are in Boston proper, not New England at large.</b> Also, it would be like looking for a needle in a haystack, pinging correct location of him. </div> </div> </div>He comes into Boston to find victims. Maybe a series of missing persons is something a Guardian might pick up on. Or, BotL has apparently murdered people who have been hunting him; again that's something they might pick up on. Or even have the unnamed hunters be other Awakened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. <b>It has nothing to my main plot of chronicle</b> - Philosophers Stone, Nicholas Flamel ( on the run ), cult of False Angel Mexeriel ( in Wendell ) or Tammuz Promethean Mr. White ( in Boston ). Adding whole Scelestus hunt to this will make plot even more convulent than it's right now - and that also only 1/4 of cabal will be actively partaking. </div> </div> </div>That's not what convoluted means. Having BotL be related to your main plot would be covoluted. There being a Scelesti that the player has to kill to pass the veil isn't convoluted; you don't need to go into his life story or explore his ideas about cannibal Jesus. You're already doing a bunch of initiations that are nothing to do with your main plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>I'm starting to think that Guardians should make one of them play Left-Handed for a bit</b> - but what this then teach to future Crimson Sister? That you cannot trust Guardians because every one of them can go Left-Hand? Even when they actively seek Left-Handed as Order's mission? </div> </div> </div>All thrones are false. Guardians are expected to watch each other.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I'd tone down BotL's arcana and gnosis a bit. He's going to stomp a new Guardian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:25:19-07:00","id":997882,"title":"","content":"I was just getting ready to answer, and here's Michael, taking words out of my mouth. I suspect &quot;Shifting Sands&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T00:12:46-07:00","id":998123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=997824#post997824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them find him. Why do you think he's in the book in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather leave him for full cabal to fight with, when/if they return to New England. He is just so great and devious NPC I would rather show him whole group, than only on PCs 'backstory'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=997824#post997824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He comes into Boston to find victims. Maybe a series of missing persons is something a Guardian might pick up on. Or, BotL has apparently murdered people who have been hunting him; again that's something they might pick up on. Or even have the unnamed hunters be other Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this seens more pluasiable. Still, I have like 2 weeks in game time till end of Orders trening of PCs, it does not look as very possible for Blood of Lamb to build proper serial killer M.O. case in to games plor.<br /> <br /> And we still want to send lone future Crimson Sister on rather powerfull Reaper and Scelastus. But thinking on this - Guardians still need to watch her then, so whole Shadow Chorus would be in nearby. Or even whenever, with their all Space shenenigans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/996624-gotv-crimson-veil?p=997824#post997824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All thrones are false. Guardians are expected to watch each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point her, I must admit. Now I'm torn between running Blood of Lamb and 'false Left-Hand Guardian' scenario...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T01:35:37-08:00","id":1025031,"title":"","content":"Interesting development on Crimson Veil plot in Boston game - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1016877-2e-bostonian-alchemist\">'black' Alchemist from Order of Golden Dawn era</a> ( she is immortal thanks to Pyros ) kidnapped cabals latest 'research project' and Guardians main problem to asses potential danger level - <i>Mr. White</i>, cabals 'friendly' Promethean. As players are about to attack Alchemist headquarter I wonder:<br /> <br /> <b>Would killing Alchemist being enough as Crimson Veil test?</b> Alchemist is sorta like Sleepwalker, working as one of 'lesser sorcerers' Orders are protecting in their extensive webs of connections. In 2E, all those like Sleepwalkers 'with minor talents' can even have Status 1 in proper Order, if they earn it. So question is - <b>Are rouge minor templates/Sleepwalkers enough targets to pass Crimson Veil if they work as target on psychological level? </b>Because 'black' Alchemists from <b>Promethean </b>sounds as good candidates for Crimson Veils all around globe.<br /> <br /> Even if answer is yes, there are other considerations in this example - <b>Do Crimson Veil killing must be alone?</b> Can future Crimson Sister be with her cabal, only that she makes the deed? <b>And what if future Crimson Sister only <i>help</i> in killing target a cabal killed - would it still be viable passing of Veil?</b><br /> <br /> If all is yes on above, there is still one large question on idea - <b>How much Guardians can inspire Crimson Sister to be on this deed?</b> Should they talk to her 'you must kill her, at all cost'? Should they just make casual reminder of principles on which Order stands and assume that Crimson Sister to be will pull the appropriate conclusions? Or should they be totally silent, with future Crimson Sister deciding completely on her own that 'black' Alchemist must die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-01-2017, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T10:19:19-08:00","id":1025102,"title":"","content":"The Crimson Veil is a test of a Guardian's ability to follow orders even to the extreme of killing someone. It's not a subtle thing, you get your orders and then you go and kill your target. Since it's also a test of moral resolve it probably has to be done alone. If you could do it by hiring a gang of thugs then you might still be able to rationalize some level of absolution from the act for yourself. Same goes if you bring along your cabal. Any potential target for being killed by the Guardians probably counts as a viable target for the Crimson Veil, in a lot of cases it's probably better for it to be someone who isn't a Mage considering that most of the time Guardian recruits are still newbie Mages. Anyway, the act isn't about the power level of the target. It's about the one being tested showing that they have the resolve to kill for the beliefs of the Guardians and also the ability to follow orders to the necessary extremes that the Guardians will push them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T12:09:12-08:00","id":1025128,"title":"","content":"Re-reading Crimson Veil section in Order book, I can see Guardians letting Red Sister to be to hunt with other of her cabal mates - they just would watch them <i>super scrupulously</i> and in final moment, isolate her with her final prey, in the end. From book looks that Guardians just will remind her about main dogma, but only if it would look like good, natural place for it - nothing forced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GotV, p. 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is for the initiate to hunt, with a team, a dangerous mage to prove the recruit\u2019s willingness to kill. The target is always a mage of some kind or, very rarely, an in\ufb02uential Sleeper. The target is never a vampire, werewolf or denizen of the Shadow Realm, no matter how useful the assassination might be. The initiate must prove himself able to kill despite identifying with the target, knowing what would<br /> and should happen to him should he ever fall to such depths. A supernatural creature is different and terrifying, and killing one does not come from the same place in one\u2019s heart or soul.<br /> <br /> Such a killing may prove something about the initiate, but does not prove what the Guardians need to know. Banishers, Seers of the Throne and rogue mages of any order (or apostates) are often the game. When the time comes, the initiate is arti\ufb01cially put into the position of having to go it alone. He believes his mentor or teammates are busy and cannot be bothered, even though they are really backing him up secretly. The Guardians of the Veil must be sure that he is not responding to any sort of pressure from his peers, that he is willing to kill for the cause and not only for his friends or teammates.<br /> (...)<br /> One important facet of the Crimson Veil is that the initiates are never <i>told </i>to kill. They are only made \ufb01rmly aware of the appropriate responses to different circumstances, then put in situations in which murder is the correct \u2014 or only \u2014 response.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}